{"version":"1","id":"beyondcode","handle":"beyondcode","name":"Beyond Code","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/97ca507b0ef34abb881caf29b0f5d4a0","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-4.1146,"y":1.5936,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":33,"newest_post_at":"2023-11-21T19:48:56.000Z","oldest_post_at":"2020-02-03T09:00:00.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.015152,"listicle_ratio":0.0,"question_ratio":0.0,"avg_read_time":3.545455,"summary_length_avg":291.40625,"title_length_avg":45.515152,"title_length_var":324.431589,"tag_entropy":2.841038,"tag_diversity":0.969697,"top_tag_share":0.060606,"avg_upvotes":2.878788,"median_upvotes":1.0,"avg_comments":0.151515,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.0625,"zero_engagement_share":0.454545,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":0.332162,"non_article_ratio":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":0.1},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[1.6029,4.9412],"cadence_depth":[-6.4118,-5.6471],"hype_variety":[3.3824,-3.5441],"title_style":[-8.0735,-0.4853]},"top_tags":[["laravel",21],["php",13],["github",4],["tailwind-css",4],["css",3],["database",3],["webdev",2],["testing",2]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["CSS to Tailwind converter \u2013 Windy","Blazing fast NodeJS dependencies with Laravel and Bun","Announcing Laravel Herd"],"outlier":["Unleash the Power of Artisan: The Laravel CLI Tool that every Laravel developer must know"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"tWjdF9kP9","title":"Creating a HelpScout app for your Laravel application","url":"https://beyondco.de/news/creating-a-helpscout-app-for-your-laravel-application","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/creating-a-helpscout-app-for-your-laravel-application-twjdf9kp9","summary":"Learn how to create a HelpScout app for your Laravel application. The app displays useful customer information and allows easy access to customer accounts.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/8839fd78e58631807d528edfd93517db?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-11-21T19:48:56.000Z"},{"id":"VxP04TTjW","title":"Testing webhooks with Expose","url":"https://beyondco.de/news/webhook-testing-with-expose","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/testing-webhooks-with-expose-vxp04ttjw","summary":"Expose is a tool that opens a secure tunnel to a global server network and forwards requests to your local machine via this tunnel. It provides a publicly accessible URL that you can use and add to the configuration of the system that is sending the webhook. Expose allows you to do this with a single click.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/0a2f5a2d1e1546e568d529060be2faff?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-09-13T08:19:50.000Z"},{"id":"GUwBBJ77y","title":"Blazing fast NodeJS dependencies with Laravel and Bun","url":"https://beyondco.de/news/using-bun-with-laravel","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/blazing-fast-nodejs-dependencies-with-laravel-and-bun-guwbbj77y","summary":"A new JavaScript tool was released in version 1.0.0 that made me get really excited. It's called Bun- an \"all-in-one toolkit for JavaScript and TypeScript apps\" You can think of it as a replacement for NPM/Yarn - but it's blazing fast.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/3396ee62d8445858198b697416b22325?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":14,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-09-11T07:53:16.000Z"},{"id":"tJTSVJ1Kg","title":"Announcing Laravel Herd","url":"https://beyondco.de/news/announcing-laravel-herd","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/announcing-laravel-herd-tjtsvj1kg","summary":"Herd is a blazing fast, native Laravel and PHP development environment for macOS. It is entirely free to download and use. Herd includes everything you need to get started with Laravel development, including PHP (versions 7.4 up to 8.3 Alpha), nginx and dnsmasq.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/bfbb344f4ab7d589a0e47d32ef248d7f?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":8,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-07-20T05:43:00.000Z"},{"id":"uRGuDKuNr","title":"Laravel Eloquent \u2013 create, update and query your database with joy","url":"https://beyondco.de/news/laravel-eloquent-create-update-and-query-your-database-with-joy","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/laravel-eloquent-create-update-and-query-your-database-with-joy-urgudkunr","summary":"Laravel Eloquent ist an object-relational-mapper, an ORM, that makes working with databases a joy. Tinkerwell uses the active record pattern where every column in the database table is accessible via a magic method.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/c5a9d61fa584db3ba8a5fd23ef1667cd?_a=AQADKdt","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-07-06T17:33:12.000Z"},{"id":"5OiPQDUBj","title":"The Importance of a Good Podcast Transcription","url":"https://beyondco.de/news/podcast-transcription","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-importance-of-a-good-podcast-transcription-5oipqdubj","summary":"A podcast transcription is a written version of a podcast episode that captures everything that was said during the recording. This text-based format allows people who cannot listen to the audio to read through the content and get the same value as someone who listened to it. Transcribe your podcast in seconds by uploading your audio file to Writeout.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1679649857/94d241a88b0cd350961a911b015a26db","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-03-24T10:22:51.000Z"},{"id":"H4B32u7uy","title":"Build a ChatGPT clone with Laravel","url":"https://beyondco.de/news/build-a-chatgpt-clone-with-laravel","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/build-a-chatgpt-clone-with-laravel-h4b32u7uy","summary":"Learn how to build a ChatGPT clone using Laravel. OpenAI has released a new AI model called gpt-3.5-turbo, which is 10 times cheaper than the DaVinci model. Prompting for this model works by sending a chat conversation to the AI model for autocompletions.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/f10dd73b343d28f857a3c6dc341fa852?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":3,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-03-03T11:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"0CDrPbKdI","title":"Query your Laravel database using natural language","url":"https://beyondco.de/news/query-your-laravel-database-using-natural-language","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/query-your-laravel-database-using-natural-language-0cdrpbkdi","summary":"Learn how to query your Laravel database using natural language with the laravel-ask-database package. Install the package, ask your database questions using natural language, and retrieve queries from natural language. The package includes security mechanisms to prevent SQL injection. The process involves creating a database query for a given question, evaluating the query, and turning the database result into an answer.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/e15828340454dbcabf6c95e5e53af590?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":6,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-02-21T11:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"5UIISYPZ-","title":"Laravel's new Process facade","url":"https://beyondco.de/news/laravel-10-new-process-facade","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/laravel-s-new-process-facade-5uiisypz","summary":"Laravel 10 introduces a new Process facade that provides syntax sugar on top of the Symfony Process component. It allows you to invoke external programs, handle their output and errors, inspect the process results, customize the process behavior, and run multiple processes in parallel. The Process facade is also easy to test and can be faked for testing purposes.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/4a885ca2a48cdacfaf7bb3108e322675?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":3,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2023-02-13T11:00:00.00